.TH JACKITNG 1 "February 2026" "JackITNG 2.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
jackitng \- Terminal-based wireless interaction and automation toolkit

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jackitng
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jackitng
is a terminal user interface (TUI) application built with Python and
Textual. It provides an interactive environment for wireless automation,
device interaction, and scripted execution workflows.

The interface is fully keyboard-driven and supports hierarchical screens
with context-aware key bindings.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B --debug
Enable debug mode with extended logging output.

.TP
.B --script PATH
Execute a script located at PATH.

.TP
.B --lowpower
Enable low power mode for reduced transmission intensity.

.TP
.B --interval INTEGER
Set execution interval in seconds.

.TP
.B --duration INTEGER
Set total execution duration in seconds.

.TP
.B --layout TEXT
Specify keyboard layout profile.

.TP
.B --address TEXT
Target specific device address.

.TP
.B --vendor TEXT
Filter or target devices by vendor name.

.TP
.B --reset
Reset device or internal state before execution.

.TP
.B --autopwn
Enable automated exploitation mode.

.TP
.B --all-channels
Scan or operate on all available channels.

.TP
.B --keylogging
Enable keylogging functionality.

.TP
.B --help
Show help message and exit.

.SH INTERFACE

The application uses a dynamic key binding system.

Bindings are defined at two levels:

.IP
1. Global bindings defined in the App class.
.br
2. Screen-specific bindings defined per active screen.

When inside a screen, screen-level bindings are displayed after
a delimiter in the footer:

.nf
Q Quit  H Help  |  ESC Close  F1 Info
.fi

Global bindings remain active at all times unless explicitly overridden.

.SH NAVIGATION

The interface is entirely keyboard-driven.

Typical controls:

.TP
.B q
Quit application.

.TP
.B ESC
Close current screen.

.TP
.B F1
Display contextual help.

Additional bindings depend on the active screen.

.SH ARCHITECTURE

.B jackitng
uses:

.IP
\- Python 3
.br
\- Textual TUI framework
.br
\- Screen stack navigation model
.br
\- Context-aware binding resolution

Bindings are resolved in the following order:

.IP
Active Screen
.br
Parent Screens
.br
Application (global)

.SH FILES

.TP
.B ~/.jackitng/
User configuration directory.

.TP
.B /usr/share/jackitng/
Shared resources.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 1
General error.

